WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.125
The best aid in any channel is a range, because it tells you exactly where the centerline is.

2
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:08.200
Look at the diagram.

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.725
A range is two fixed marks.

4
00:00:10.975 --> 00:00:13.425
The front one is lower and nearer.

5
00:00:13.675 --> 00:00:16.475
The rear one is higher and farther away.

6
00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:20.700
When the two line up, one above the other, you’re on the centerline.

7
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.650
And when they don’t?

8
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.150
Say the rear mark shows to the right of the front one.

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.450
You’re to the left of the line.

10
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.675
So steer right, until they close up again.

11
00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:34.750
Here’s the handle: follow the rear mark.

12
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.575
A range gives you something else for free.

13
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:45.000
The chart prints the range’s true direction, so every time you’re lined up, you can check your compass.

14
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.950
One caution.

15
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.625
A range line keeps going after the channel ends.

16
00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:55.600
Use it only within the charted channel, or it will lead you straight aground.
